```

`stopComment(report, prNumber, agent?)` — mention the agent when it was started. But careful: the comment text goes to the notice, and the agent is dispatched on the PR. The comment should say "an agent (`engineer`) has been started on #N to resolve them". Signature: `stopComment(report, prNumber, agent = "")`.

Also `updateBody(report)` — "updateBody / stopComment 文言にエージェントを記述". updateBody should say that an agent will be started when conflicts + pr-agent. But updateBody is called before the dispatch decision, and it needs the agent name. So `updateBody(report, agent?)` where agent is the conflict agent name when mode is pr-agent. Then the body says "the machinery starts `<agent>` on this pull request to resolve them" vs. "comment and ask an agent".

Now: where does updateBody get called? Line 467 & 486. I'll compute `const conflictAgent = getNewReleaseMode() === "pr-agent" ? getUpdateConflictAgent() : "";` earlier (right after report is built, before the PR create), pass into updateBody. Then use it at the conflict branch.

Note configProblems guarantees the agent exists when pr-agent; in a tree where the key is missing, `getUpdateConflictAgent()` returns "" → no dispatch. Good fallback (no crash).

Now `getNewReleaseMode` type: `"issue" | "pr" | "pr-agent"`. config.ts reader:

```ts
export type NewReleaseMode = "issue" | "pr" | "pr-agent";

export function getNewReleaseMode(fallback: NewReleaseMode = "issue"): NewReleaseMode {
  const value = loadConfig().update?.on_new_release;
  return value === "pr" || value === "pr-agent" ? value : fallback;
}
```
Hmm — if invalid value, fallback to issue. configProblems reports it. Simple: `return value ?? fallback` typed. But a YAML `on_new_release: Pr` would then be an invalid union at runtime. Use the explicit check to be safe: unknown → fallback. Actually, being strict (returning the raw string) would make dispatch decisions on garbage. Explicit check is better; comment why: an unrecognised value is reported by `configProblems`, and the reader treats it as the default rather than acting on a value it does not understand.

And:
```ts
export function getUpdateConflictAgent(): string {
  return (loadConfig().agents?.on_update_conflict ?? "").trim();
}
```

Now notify side needs `getNewReleaseMode` too. And the branch name: import `updateBranchFor` from update_atomaton? That's a script module importing another script module — notify test imports NOTICE_MARKER from notify already, so it's an accepted pattern. But cleaner: `updateBranchFor` is a pure function about the update lane; move it to `lib/pr-head-branch.ts`? There is already `lib/pr-head-branch.ts`! Let me look — it may already hold branch naming helpers.

